IMPORT prelude

-- War Gratuity Act 1945 (Cth) — THE NOUNS, THE RULES AND THE TOP-LEVEL GOAL.
-- Source: ../registers/source-bundle/C1945A00016.txt (compilation No. 4, 21
-- October 2016). The Second World War veteran, or their dependants, ask:
-- "How much war gratuity is to be credited for my service?" Amounts are in
-- decimal dollars, as the compilation prints them.

§ `Nouns`

-- s 13: whether the member died of war service, and in what service.
DECLARE `Death` IS ONE OF
    `the member did not die of war service`
    `died of war service while in overseas qualifying service`
    `died of war service while in other general qualifying service`

DECLARE `Gratuity case` HAS
    -- ss 7, 9-11: days of qualifying service (general includes overseas)
    `days of overseas qualifying service`                           IS A NUMBER
    `days of general qualifying service`                            IS A NUMBER
    -- s 8
    `I returned at my own request, for discipline, or for an excepted injury or illness` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the death`                                                     IS A `Death`
    -- s 14
    `someone was totally dependent on the member, who died before 1 July 1947` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 15 and the Schedule
    `the member is in a disqualified class`                         IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 16
    `debts to deduct`                                               IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `Gratuity position` HAS
    `months at the overseas rate`                                   IS A NUMBER
    `months at the general rate`                                    IS A NUMBER
    `the war gratuity in dollars`                                   IS A NUMBER
    `it is a free gift that may be withheld or deferred`            IS A BOOLEAN

§ `Rules`

-- s 2 month: 30 days; s 12: any fraction counts as a month.
@ref ss 2 month, 12
GIVEN days IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`months in` days MEANS
    IF days AT MOST 0 THEN 0
    ELSE IF FLOOR (days DIVIDED BY 30) EQUALS days DIVIDED BY 30
         THEN days DIVIDED BY 30
         ELSE FLOOR (days DIVIDED BY 30) PLUS 1

-- s 12(1) with s 8: fewer than 12 months of overseas qualifying service count
-- as 12, unless the member came back at their own request, for discipline or
-- for an excepted injury or illness.
@ref ss 8, 12(1)
GIVEN c IS A `Gratuity case`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the overseas months for` c MEANS
    IF     raw GREATER THAN 0
       AND raw LESS THAN 12
       AND NOT (c's `I returned at my own request, for discipline, or for an excepted injury or illness`)
    THEN 12
    ELSE raw
    WHERE
        raw MEANS `months in` (c's `days of overseas qualifying service`)

-- s 12(2): general months less the overseas months, not below nil.
@ref s 12(2)
GIVEN c IS A `Gratuity case`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the general months for` c MEANS
    IF `months in` (c's `days of general qualifying service`) GREATER THAN `the overseas months for` c
    THEN `months in` (c's `days of general qualifying service`) MINUS `the overseas months for` c
    ELSE 0

-- s 4: $7.50 a month overseas, $1.50 a month general; s 13: 7 more months at
-- the rate of the service in which the member died of war service.
@ref ss 4, 13
GIVEN c IS A `Gratuity case`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the gratuity before the minimum for` c MEANS
    750/100 TIMES `the overseas months for` c
    PLUS 150/100 TIMES `the general months for` c
    PLUS (CONSIDER c's `the death`
          WHEN `died of war service while in overseas qualifying service` THEN 750/100 TIMES 7
          WHEN `died of war service while in other general qualifying service` THEN 150/100 TIMES 7
          WHEN `the member did not die of war service` THEN 0)

-- s 14: at least 3 years at the overseas rate ($270) where someone was totally
-- dependent on a member who died of war service before 1 July 1947.
@ref s 14
GIVEN c IS A `Gratuity case`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the gratuity after the minimum for` c MEANS
    IF     c's `someone was totally dependent on the member, who died before 1 July 1947`
       AND NOT (c's `the death` EQUALS `the member did not die of war service`)
       AND `the gratuity before the minimum for` c LESS THAN 750/100 TIMES 36
    THEN 750/100 TIMES 36
    ELSE `the gratuity before the minimum for` c

-- s 15: none for a disqualified class (subject to a prescribed authority's
-- discretion); s 16: debts deducted, not below nil.
@ref ss 15, 16
GIVEN c IS A `Gratuity case`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the war gratuity for` c MEANS
    IF c's `the member is in a disqualified class`
    THEN 0
    ELSE IF `the gratuity after the minimum for` c GREATER THAN c's `debts to deduct`
         THEN `the gratuity after the minimum for` c MINUS c's `debts to deduct`
         ELSE 0

@ref ss 4, 6, 8, 12-16
@export default The war gratuity to be credited for a Second World War member's service under the War Gratuity Act 1945 (Cth): $7.50 a month of overseas qualifying service and $1.50 a month of the rest of general qualifying service, counting 30-day months with any fraction as a month (ss 4, 12); at least 12 months overseas unless the member came back at their own request, for discipline or for an excepted injury or illness (s 8); 7 more months at the rate of the service in which a member died of war service (s 13); at least 3 years at the overseas rate where a dependant was totally dependent on a member who died before 1 July 1947 (s 14); none for a disqualified class (s 15); less fraud and repatriation debts (s 16). It is a free gift, which a prescribed authority may withhold or defer (s 6). DRAFT, not reviewed by an Australian lawyer.
GIVEN c IS A `Gratuity case`  @desc The days of overseas and general qualifying service, any return or death, total dependency, disqualification and debts
GIVETH A `Gratuity position`
`the gratuity position for` c MEANS
    `Gratuity position` OF `the overseas months for` c, `the general months for` c, `the war gratuity for` c, TRUE
